            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-10735-libpython2.7-stdlib",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-10735 high vulnerability for libpython2.7-stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in python. In algorithms with quadratic time complexity using non-binary bases, when using int(\"text\"), a system could take 50ms to parse an int string with 100,000 digits and 5s for 1,000,000 digits (float, decimal, int.from_bytes(), and int() for binary bases 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 are not affected). The highest threat from this vulnerability is to system availability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-10735\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libpython2.7-stdlib\nVersion: 2.7.16-2+deb10u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/libpython2.7-stdlib/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2020-10735](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-10735)",
