                "text": "In WriteOnePNGImage() of the PNG coder at coders/png.c, an improper call to AcquireVirtualMemory() and memset() allows for an out-of-bounds write later when PopShortPixel() from MagickCore/quantum-private.h is called. The patch fixes the calls by adding 256 to rowbytes. An attacker who is able to supply a specially crafted image could affect availability with a low impact to data integrity. This flaw affects ImageMagick versions prior to 6.9.10-68 and 7.0.8-68."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-25664\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libmagickwand-6-headers\nVersion: 8:6.9.10.23+dfsg-2.1+deb10u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/libmagickwand-6-headers/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2020-25664](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-25664)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2020-25664**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libmagickwand-6-headers  | 8:6.9.10.23+dfsg-2.1+deb10u5  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/libmagickwand-6-headers/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2020-25664](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-25664)  |\n"
