            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-27753-imagemagick",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-27753 low vulnerability for imagemagick package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There are several memory leaks in the MIFF coder in /coders/miff.c due to improper image depth values, which can be triggered by a specially crafted input file. These leaks could potentially lead to an impact to application availability or cause a denial of service. It was originally reported that the issues were in `AcquireMagickMemory()` because that is where LeakSanitizer detected the leaks, but the patch resolves issues in the MIFF coder, which incorrectly handles data being passed to `AcquireMagickMemory()`. This flaw affects ImageMagick versions prior to 7.0.9-0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-27753\nSeverity: low\nPackage: imagemagick\nVersion: 8:6.9.10.23+dfsg-2.1+deb10u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/imagemagick/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2020-27753](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-27753)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2020-27753**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | imagemagick  | 8:6.9.10.23+dfsg-2.1+deb10u5  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/imagemagick/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2020-27753](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-27753)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
