              "id": "CVE-2021-20294-binutils-x86-64-linux-gnu",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-20294 low vulnerability for binutils-x86-64-linux-gnu package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in binutils readelf 2.35 program. An attacker who is able to convince a victim using readelf to read a crafted file could trigger a stack buffer overflow, out-of-bounds write of arbitrary data supplied by the attacker. The highest impact of this flaw is to confidentiality, integrity, and availability."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-20294\nSeverity: low\nPackage: binutils-x86-64-linux-gnu\nVersion: 2.31.1-16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/binutils-x86-64-linux-gnu/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-20294](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-20294)",
