            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47253-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47253 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  drm/amd/display: Fix potential memory leak in DMUB hw_init  [Why] On resume we perform DMUB hw_init which allocates memory: dm_resume-\u003edm_dmub_hw_init-\u003edc_dmub_srv_create-\u003ekzalloc That results in memory leak in suspend/resume scenarios.  [How] Allocate memory for the DC wrapper to DMUB only if it was not allocated before. No need to reallocate it on suspend/resume."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47253\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47253](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47253)",
