            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47281-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47281 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ALSA: seq: Fix race of snd_seq_timer_open()  The timer instance per queue is exclusive, and snd_seq_timer_open() should have managed the concurrent accesses.  It looks as if it's checking the already existing timer instance at the beginning, but it's not right, because there is no protection, hence any later concurrent call of snd_seq_timer_open() may override the timer instance easily.  This may result in UAF, as the leftover timer instance can keep running while the queue itself gets closed, as spotted by syzkaller recently.  For avoiding the race, add a proper check at the assignment of tmr-\u003etimeri again, and return -EBUSY if it's been already registered."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47281\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47281](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47281)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47281**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47281](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47281)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47283-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47283 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  net:sfc: fix non-freed irq in legacy irq mode  SFC driver can be configured via modparam to work using MSI-X, MSI or legacy IRQ interrupts. In the last one, the interrupt was not properly released on module remove.  It was not freed because the flag irqs_hooked was not set during initialization in the case of using legacy IRQ.  Example of (trimmed) trace during module remove without this fix:  remove_proc_entry: removing non-empty directory 'irq/125', leaking at least '0000:3b:00.1' WARNING: CPU: 39 PID: 3658 at fs/proc/generic.c:715 remove_proc_entry+0x15c/0x170 ...trimmed... Call Trace:  unregister_irq_proc+0xe3/0x100  free_desc+0x29/0x70  irq_free_descs+0x47/0x70  mp_unmap_irq+0x58/0x60  acpi_unregister_gsi_ioapic+0x2a/0x40  acpi_pci_irq_disable+0x78/0xb0  pci_disable_device+0xd1/0x100  efx_pci_remove+0xa1/0x1e0 [sfc]  pci_device_remove+0x38/0xa0  __device_release_driver+0x177/0x230  driver_detach+0xcb/0x110  bus_remove_driver+0x58/0xd0  pci_unregister_driver+0x2a/0xb0  efx_exit_module+0x24/0xf40 [sfc]  __do_sys_delete_module.constprop.0+0x171/0x280  ? exit_to_user_mode_prepare+0x83/0x1d0  do_syscall_64+0x3d/0x80  entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x44/0xae RIP: 0033:0x7f9f9385800b ...trimmed..."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47283\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47283](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47283)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47283**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47283](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47283)  |\n"
