            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47467-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47467 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  kunit: fix reference count leak in kfree_at_end  The reference counting issue happens in the normal path of kfree_at_end(). When kunit_alloc_and_get_resource() is invoked, the function forgets to handle the returned resource object, whose refcount increased inside, causing a refcount leak.  Fix this issue by calling kunit_alloc_resource() instead of kunit_alloc_and_get_resource().  Fixed the following when applying: Shuah Khan \u003cskhan@linuxfoundation.org\u003e  CHECK: Alignment should match open parenthesis +\tkunit_alloc_resource(test, NULL, kfree_res_free, GFP_KERNEL,  \t\t\t\t     (void *)to_free);"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47467\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47467](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47467)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47467**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47467](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47467)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47469-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47469 low vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  spi: Fix deadlock when adding SPI controllers on SPI buses  Currently we have a global spi_add_lock which we take when adding new devices so that we can check that we're not trying to reuse a chip select that's already controlled.  This means that if the SPI device is itself a SPI controller and triggers the instantiation of further SPI devices we trigger a deadlock as we try to register and instantiate those devices while in the process of doing so for the parent controller and hence already holding the global spi_add_lock.  Since we only care about concurrency within a single SPI bus move the lock to be per controller, avoiding the deadlock.  This can be easily triggered in the case of spi-mux."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47469\nSeverity: low\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47469](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47469)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47469**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47469](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47469)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47473-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47473 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  scsi: qla2xxx: Fix a memory leak in an error path of qla2x00_process_els()  Commit 8c0eb596baa5 (\"[SCSI] qla2xxx: Fix a memory leak in an error path of qla2x00_process_els()\"), intended to change:          bsg_job-\u003erequest-\u003emsgcode == FC_BSG_HST_ELS_NOLOGIN           bsg_job-\u003erequest-\u003emsgcode != FC_BSG_RPT_ELS  but changed it to:          bsg_job-\u003erequest-\u003emsgcode == FC_BSG_RPT_ELS  instead.  Change the == to a != to avoid leaking the fcport structure or freeing unallocated memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47473\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47473](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47473)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47473**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47473](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47473)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
