              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47479-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47479 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  staging: rtl8712: fix use-after-free in rtl8712_dl_fw  Syzbot reported use-after-free in rtl8712_dl_fw(). The problem was in race condition between r871xu_dev_remove() -\u003endo_open() callback.  It's easy to see from crash log, that driver accesses released firmware in -\u003endo_open() callback. It may happen, since driver was releasing firmware _before_ unregistering netdev. Fix it by moving unregister_netdev() before cleaning up resources.  Call Trace: ...  rtl871x_open_fw drivers/staging/rtl8712/hal_init.c:83 [inline]  rtl8712_dl_fw+0xd95/0xe10 drivers/staging/rtl8712/hal_init.c:170  rtl8712_hal_init drivers/staging/rtl8712/hal_init.c:330 [inline]  rtl871x_hal_init+0xae/0x180 drivers/staging/rtl8712/hal_init.c:394  netdev_open+0xe6/0x6c0 drivers/staging/rtl8712/os_intfs.c:380  __dev_open+0x2bc/0x4d0 net/core/dev.c:1484  Freed by task 1306: ...  release_firmware+0x1b/0x30 drivers/base/firmware_loader/main.c:1053  r871xu_dev_remove+0xcc/0x2c0 drivers/staging/rtl8712/usb_intf.c:599  usb_unbind_interface+0x1d8/0x8d0 drivers/usb/core/driver.c:458"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47479\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47479](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47479)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47479**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47479](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47479)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47490-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47490 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  drm/ttm: fix memleak in ttm_transfered_destroy  We need to cleanup the fences for ghost objects as well.  Bug: https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214029 Bug: https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214447"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47490\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47490](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47490)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47490**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47490](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47490)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
