              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47493-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47493 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ocfs2: fix race between searching chunks and release journal_head from buffer_head  Encountered a race between ocfs2_test_bg_bit_allocatable() and jbd2_journal_put_journal_head() resulting in the below vmcore.    PID: 106879  TASK: ffff880244ba9c00  CPU: 2   COMMAND: \"loop3\"   Call trace:     panic     oops_end     no_context     __bad_area_nosemaphore     bad_area_nosemaphore     __do_page_fault     do_page_fault     page_fault       [exception RIP: ocfs2_block_group_find_clear_bits+316]     ocfs2_block_group_find_clear_bits [ocfs2]     ocfs2_cluster_group_search [ocfs2]     ocfs2_search_chain [ocfs2]     ocfs2_claim_suballoc_bits [ocfs2]     __ocfs2_claim_clusters [ocfs2]     ocfs2_claim_clusters [ocfs2]     ocfs2_local_alloc_slide_window [ocfs2]     ocfs2_reserve_local_alloc_bits [ocfs2]     ocfs2_reserve_clusters_with_limit [ocfs2]     ocfs2_reserve_clusters [ocfs2]     ocfs2_lock_refcount_allocators [ocfs2]     ocfs2_make_clusters_writable [ocfs2]     ocfs2_replace_cow [ocfs2]     ocfs2_refcount_cow [ocfs2]     ocfs2_file_write_iter [ocfs2]     lo_rw_aio     loop_queue_work     kthread_worker_fn     kthread     ret_from_fork  When ocfs2_test_bg_bit_allocatable() called bh2jh(bg_bh), the bg_bh-\u003eb_private NULL as jbd2_journal_put_journal_head() raced and released the jounal head from the buffer head.  Needed to take bit lock for the bit 'BH_JournalHead' to fix this race."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47493\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47493](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47493)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47493**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47493](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47493)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "4.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47496-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47496 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  net/tls: Fix flipped sign in tls_err_abort() calls  sk-\u003esk_err appears to expect a positive value, a convention that ktls doesn't always follow and that leads to memory corruption in other code. For instance,      [kworker]     tls_encrypt_done(..., err=\u003cnegative error from crypto request\u003e)       tls_err_abort(.., err)         sk-\u003esk_err = err;      [task]     splice_from_pipe_feed       ...         tls_sw_do_sendpage           if (sk-\u003esk_err) {             ret = -sk-\u003esk_err;  // ret is positive      splice_from_pipe_feed (continued)       ret = actor(...)  // ret is still positive and interpreted as bytes                         // written, resulting in underflow of buf-\u003elen and                         // sd-\u003elen, leading to huge buf-\u003eoffset and bogus                         // addresses computed in later calls to actor()  Fix all tls_err_abort() callers to pass a negative error code consistently and centralize the error-prone sign flip there, throwing in a warning to catch future misuse and uninlining the function so it really does only warn once."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47496\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47496](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47496)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2021-47496**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2021-47496](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47496)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2021-47498-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2021-47498 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  dm rq: don't queue request to blk-mq during DM suspend  DM uses blk-mq's quiesce/unquiesce to stop/start device mapper queue.  But blk-mq's unquiesce may come from outside events, such as elevator switch, updating nr_requests or others, and request may come during suspend, so simply ask for blk-mq to requeue it.  Fixes one kernel panic issue when running updating nr_requests and dm-mpath suspend/resume stress test."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2021-47498\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2021-47498](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2021-47498)",
