              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-48699-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-48699 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  sched/debug: fix dentry leak in update_sched_domain_debugfs  Kuyo reports that the pattern of using debugfs_remove(debugfs_lookup()) leaks a dentry and with a hotplug stress test, the machine eventually runs out of memory.  Fix this up by using the newly created debugfs_lookup_and_remove() call instead which properly handles the dentry reference counting logic."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-48699\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2022-48699](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-48699)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-48699**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2022-48699](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-48699)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
