              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-48700-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-48700 low vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  vfio/type1: Unpin zero pages  There's currently a reference count leak on the zero page.  We increment the reference via pin_user_pages_remote(), but the page is later handled as an invalid/reserved page, therefore it's not accounted against the user and not unpinned by our put_pfn().  Introducing special zero page handling in put_pfn() would resolve the leak, but without accounting of the zero page, a single user could still create enough mappings to generate a reference count overflow.  The zero page is always resident, so for our purposes there's no reason to keep it pinned.  Therefore, add a loop to walk pages returned from pin_user_pages_remote() and unpin any zero pages."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-48700\nSeverity: low\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2022-48700](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-48700)",
