            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27043-libpython2.7-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27043 medium vulnerability for libpython2.7-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The email module of Python through 3.11.3 incorrectly parses e-mail addresses that contain a special character. The wrong portion of an RFC2822 header is identified as the value of the addr-spec. In some applications, an attacker can bypass a protection mechanism in which application access is granted only after verifying receipt of e-mail to a specific domain (e.g., only @company.example.com addresses may be used for signup). This occurs in email/_parseaddr.py in recent versions of Python."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-27043\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython2.7-minimal\nVersion: 2.7.16-2+deb10u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/libpython2.7-minimal/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-27043](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-27043)",
