              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-4244-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-4244 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use-after-free vulnerability in the Linux kernel's netfilter: nf_tables component can be exploited to achieve local privilege escalation.  Due to a race condition between nf_tables netlink control plane transaction and nft_set element garbage collection, it is possible to underflow the reference counter causing a use-after-free vulnerability.  We recommend upgrading past commit 3e91b0ebd994635df2346353322ac51ce84ce6d8."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-4244\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.304-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-4244](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-4244)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-4244**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.304-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-4244](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-4244)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-42753-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-42753 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An array indexing vulnerability was found in the netfilter subsystem of the Linux kernel. A missing macro could lead to a miscalculation of the `h-\u003enets` array offset, providing attackers with the primitive to arbitrarily increment/decrement a memory buffer out-of-bound. This issue may allow a local user to crash the system or potentially escalate their privileges on the system."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
