            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-50868-libsystemd0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-50868 high vulnerability for libsystemd0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Closest Encloser Proof aspect of the DNS protocol (in RFC 5155 when RFC 9276 guidance is skipped) allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption for SHA-1 computations) via DNSSEC responses in a random subdomain attack, aka the \"NSEC3\" issue. The RFC 5155 specification implies that an algorithm must perform thousands of iterations of a hash function in certain situations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-50868\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libsystemd0\nVersion: 241-7~deb10u10\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/libsystemd0/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-50868](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-50868)",
