            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52504-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52504 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  x86/alternatives: Disable KASAN in apply_alternatives()  Fei has reported that KASAN triggers during apply_alternatives() on a 5-level paging machine:  \tBUG: KASAN: out-of-bounds in rcu_is_watching() \tRead of size 4 at addr ff110003ee6419a0 by task swapper/0/0 \t... \t__asan_load4() \trcu_is_watching() \ttrace_hardirqs_on() \ttext_poke_early() \tapply_alternatives() \t...  On machines with 5-level paging, cpu_feature_enabled(X86_FEATURE_LA57) gets patched. It includes KASAN code, where KASAN_SHADOW_START depends on __VIRTUAL_MASK_SHIFT, which is defined with cpu_feature_enabled().  KASAN gets confused when apply_alternatives() patches the KASAN_SHADOW_START users. A test patch that makes KASAN_SHADOW_START static, by replacing __VIRTUAL_MASK_SHIFT with 56, works around the issue.  Fix it for real by disabling KASAN while the kernel is patching alternatives.  [ mingo: updated the changelog ]"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52504\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.304-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52504](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52504)",
