            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52583-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52583 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ceph: fix deadlock or deadcode of misusing dget()  The lock order is incorrect between denty and its parent, we should always make sure that the parent get the lock first.  But since this deadcode is never used and the parent dir will always be set from the callers, let's just remove it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52583\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52583](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52583)",
