            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52586-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52586 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  drm/msm/dpu: Add mutex lock in control vblank irq  Add a mutex lock to control vblank irq to synchronize vblank enable/disable operations happening from different threads to prevent race conditions while registering/unregistering the vblank irq callback.  v4: -Removed vblank_ctl_lock from dpu_encoder_virt, so it is only a     parameter of dpu_encoder_phys.     -Switch from atomic refcnt to a simple int counter as mutex has     now been added v3: Mistakenly did not change wording in last version. It is done now. v2: Slightly changed wording of commit message  Patchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/571854/"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52586\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52586](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52586)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-52586**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-52586](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52586)  |\n"
