              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52594-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52594 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  wifi: ath9k: Fix potential array-index-out-of-bounds read in ath9k_htc_txstatus()  Fix an array-index-out-of-bounds read in ath9k_htc_txstatus(). The bug occurs when txs-\u003ecnt, data from a URB provided by a USB device, is bigger than the size of the array txs-\u003etxstatus, which is HTC_MAX_TX_STATUS. WARN_ON() already checks it, but there is no bug handling code after the check. Make the function return if that is the case.  Found by a modified version of syzkaller.  UBSAN: array-index-out-of-bounds in htc_drv_txrx.c index 13 is out of range for type '__wmi_event_txstatus [12]' Call Trace:  ath9k_htc_txstatus  ath9k_wmi_event_tasklet  tasklet_action_common  __do_softirq  irq_exit_rxu  sysvec_apic_timer_interrupt"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52594\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52594](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52594)",
