            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52609-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52609 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  binder: fix race between mmput() and do_exit()  Task A calls binder_update_page_range() to allocate and insert pages on a remote address space from Task B. For this, Task A pins the remote mm via mmget_not_zero() first. This can race with Task B do_exit() and the final mmput() refcount decrement will come from Task A.    Task A            | Task B   ------------------+------------------   mmget_not_zero()  |                     |  do_exit()                     |    exit_mm()                     |      mmput()   mmput()           |     exit_mmap()     |       remove_vma()  |         fput()      |  In this case, the work of ____fput() from Task B is queued up in Task A as TWA_RESUME. So in theory, Task A returns to userspace and the cleanup work gets executed. However, Task A instead sleep, waiting for a reply from Task B that never comes (it's dead).  This means the binder_deferred_release() is blocked until an unrelated binder event forces Task A to go back to userspace. All the associated death notifications will also be delayed until then.  In order to fix this use mmput_async() that will schedule the work in the corresponding mm-\u003easync_put_work WQ instead of Task A."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52609\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52609](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52609)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-52609**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-52609](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52609)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "4.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52612-linux-libc-dev",
