              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52615-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52615 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  hwrng: core - Fix page fault dead lock on mmap-ed hwrng  There is a dead-lock in the hwrng device read path.  This triggers when the user reads from /dev/hwrng into memory also mmap-ed from /dev/hwrng.  The resulting page fault triggers a recursive read which then dead-locks.  Fix this by using a stack buffer when calling copy_to_user."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52615\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52615](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52615)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-52615**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-52615](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52615)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
