            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52622-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52622 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ext4: avoid online resizing failures due to oversized flex bg  When we online resize an ext4 filesystem with a oversized flexbg_size,       mkfs.ext4 -F -G 67108864 $dev -b 4096 100M      mount $dev $dir      resize2fs $dev 16G  the following WARN_ON is triggered: ================================================================== WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 427 at mm/page_alloc.c:4402 __alloc_pages+0x411/0x550 Modules linked in: sg(E) CPU: 0 PID: 427 Comm: resize2fs Tainted: G  E  6.6.0-rc5+ #314 RIP: 0010:__alloc_pages+0x411/0x550 Call Trace:  \u003cTASK\u003e  __kmalloc_large_node+0xa2/0x200  __kmalloc+0x16e/0x290  ext4_resize_fs+0x481/0xd80  __ext4_ioctl+0x1616/0x1d90  ext4_ioctl+0x12/0x20  __x64_sys_ioctl+0xf0/0x150  do_syscall_64+0x3b/0x90 ==================================================================  This is because flexbg_size is too large and the size of the new_group_data array to be allocated exceeds MAX_ORDER. Currently, the minimum value of MAX_ORDER is 8, the minimum value of PAGE_SIZE is 4096, the corresponding maximum number of groups that can be allocated is:   (PAGE_SIZE \u003c\u003c MAX_ORDER) / sizeof(struct ext4_new_group_data) ≈ 21845  And the value that is down-aligned to the power of 2 is 16384. Therefore, this value is defined as MAX_RESIZE_BG, and the number of groups added each time does not exceed this value during resizing, and is added multiple times to complete the online resizing. The difference is that the metadata in a flex_bg may be more dispersed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52622\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52622](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52622)",
