            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52653-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52653 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  SUNRPC: fix a memleak in gss_import_v2_context  The ctx-\u003emech_used.data allocated by kmemdup is not freed in neither gss_import_v2_context nor it only caller gss_krb5_import_sec_context, which frees ctx on error.  Thus, this patch reform the last call of gss_import_v2_context to the gss_krb5_import_ctx_v2, preventing the memleak while keepping the return formation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52653\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52653](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52653)",
