            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52810-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52810 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  fs/jfs: Add check for negative db_l2nbperpage  l2nbperpage is log2(number of blks per page), and the minimum legal value should be 0, not negative.  In the case of l2nbperpage being negative, an error will occur when subsequently used as shift exponent.  Syzbot reported this bug:  UBSAN: shift-out-of-bounds in fs/jfs/jfs_dmap.c:799:12 shift exponent -16777216 is negative"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52810\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.304-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52810](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52810)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-52810**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.304-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-52810](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52810)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52811-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-52811 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  scsi: ibmvfc: Remove BUG_ON in the case of an empty event pool  In practice the driver should never send more commands than are allocated to a queue's event pool. In the unlikely event that this happens, the code asserts a BUG_ON, and in the case that the kernel is not configured to crash on panic returns a junk event pointer from the empty event list causing things to spiral from there. This BUG_ON is a historical artifact of the ibmvfc driver first being upstreamed, and it is well known now that the use of BUG_ON is bad practice except in the most unrecoverable scenario. There is nothing about this scenario that prevents the driver from recovering and carrying on.  Remove the BUG_ON in question from ibmvfc_get_event() and return a NULL pointer in the case of an empty event pool. Update all call sites to ibmvfc_get_event() to check for a NULL pointer and perfrom the appropriate failure or recovery action."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-52811\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2023-52811](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52811)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-52811**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2023-52811](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-52811)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-52812-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
