            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26752-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26752 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  l2tp: pass correct message length to ip6_append_data  l2tp_ip6_sendmsg needs to avoid accounting for the transport header twice when splicing more data into an already partially-occupied skbuff.  To manage this, we check whether the skbuff contains data using skb_queue_empty when deciding how much data to append using ip6_append_data.  However, the code which performed the calculation was incorrect:       ulen = len + skb_queue_empty(\u0026sk-\u003esk_write_queue) ? transhdrlen : 0;  ...due to C operator precedence, this ends up setting ulen to transhdrlen for messages with a non-zero length, which results in corrupted packets on the wire.  Add parentheses to correct the calculation in line with the original intent."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26752\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26752](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26752)",
