              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26773-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26773 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ext4: avoid allocating blocks from corrupted group in ext4_mb_try_best_found()  Determine if the group block bitmap is corrupted before using ac_b_ex in ext4_mb_try_best_found() to avoid allocating blocks from a group with a corrupted block bitmap in the following concurrency and making the situation worse.  ext4_mb_regular_allocator   ext4_lock_group(sb, group)   ext4_mb_good_group    // check if the group bbitmap is corrupted   ext4_mb_complex_scan_group    // Scan group gets ac_b_ex but doesn't use it   ext4_unlock_group(sb, group)                            ext4_mark_group_bitmap_corrupted(group)                            // The block bitmap was corrupted during                            // the group unlock gap.   ext4_mb_try_best_found     ext4_lock_group(ac-\u003eac_sb, group)     ext4_mb_use_best_found       mb_mark_used       // Allocating blocks in block bitmap corrupted group"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26773\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26773](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26773)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26773**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26773](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26773)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26774-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26774 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ext4: avoid dividing by 0 in mb_update_avg_fragment_size() when block bitmap corrupt  Determine if bb_fragments is 0 instead of determining bb_free to eliminate the risk of dividing by zero when the block bitmap is corrupted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26774\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26774](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26774)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26774**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26774](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26774)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
