              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26775-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26775 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  aoe: avoid potential deadlock at set_capacity  Move set_capacity() outside of the section procected by (\u0026d-\u003elock). To avoid possible interrupt unsafe locking scenario:          CPU0                    CPU1         ----                    ---- [1] lock(\u0026bdev-\u003ebd_size_lock);                                 local_irq_disable();                             [2] lock(\u0026d-\u003elock);                             [3] lock(\u0026bdev-\u003ebd_size_lock);    \u003cInterrupt\u003e [4]  lock(\u0026d-\u003elock);    *** DEADLOCK ***  Where [1](\u0026bdev-\u003ebd_size_lock) hold by zram_add()-\u003eset_capacity(). [2]lock(\u0026d-\u003elock) hold by aoeblk_gdalloc(). And aoeblk_gdalloc() is trying to acquire [3](\u0026bdev-\u003ebd_size_lock) at set_capacity() call. In this situation an attempt to acquire [4]lock(\u0026d-\u003elock) from aoecmd_cfg_rsp() will lead to deadlock.  So the simplest solution is breaking lock dependency [2](\u0026d-\u003elock) -\u003e [3](\u0026bdev-\u003ebd_size_lock) by moving set_capacity() outside."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26775\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26775](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26775)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26775**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26775](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26775)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26776-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26776 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  spi: hisi-sfc-v3xx: Return IRQ_NONE if no interrupts were detected  Return IRQ_NONE from the interrupt handler when no interrupt was detected. Because an empty interrupt will cause a null pointer error:      Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual   address 0000000000000008     Call trace:         complete+0x54/0x100         hisi_sfc_v3xx_isr+0x2c/0x40 [spi_hisi_sfc_v3xx]         __handle_irq_event_percpu+0x64/0x1e0         handle_irq_event+0x7c/0x1cc"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26776\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26776](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26776)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26776**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26776](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26776)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26777-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26777 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  fbdev: sis: Error out if pixclock equals zero  The userspace program could pass any values to the driver through ioctl() interface. If the driver doesn't check the value of pixclock, it may cause divide-by-zero error.  In sisfb_check_var(), var-\u003epixclock is used as a divisor to caculate drate before it is checked against zero. Fix this by checking it at the beginning.  This is similar to CVE-2022-3061 in i740fb which was fixed by commit 15cf0b8."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26777\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26777](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26777)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26777**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26777](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26777)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26778-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26778 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  fbdev: savage: Error out if pixclock equals zero  The userspace program could pass any values to the driver through ioctl() interface. If the driver doesn't check the value of pixclock, it may cause divide-by-zero error.  Although pixclock is checked in savagefb_decode_var(), but it is not checked properly in savagefb_probe(). Fix this by checking whether pixclock is zero in the function savagefb_check_var() before info-\u003evar.pixclock is used as the divisor.  This is similar to CVE-2022-3061 in i740fb which was fixed by commit 15cf0b8."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26778\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26778](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26778)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26778**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26778](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26778)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
