            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26894-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26894 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ACPI: processor_idle: Fix memory leak in acpi_processor_power_exit()  After unregistering the CPU idle device, the memory associated with it is not freed, leading to a memory leak:  unreferenced object 0xffff896282f6c000 (size 1024):   comm \"swapper/0\", pid 1, jiffies 4294893170   hex dump (first 32 bytes):     00 00 00 00 0b 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................     00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  ................   backtrace (crc 8836a742):     [\u003cffffffff993495ed\u003e] kmalloc_trace+0x29d/0x340     [\u003cffffffff9972f3b3\u003e] acpi_processor_power_init+0xf3/0x1c0     [\u003cffffffff9972d263\u003e] __acpi_processor_start+0xd3/0xf0     [\u003cffffffff9972d2bc\u003e] acpi_processor_start+0x2c/0x50     [\u003cffffffff99805872\u003e] really_probe+0xe2/0x480     [\u003cffffffff99805c98\u003e] __driver_probe_device+0x78/0x160     [\u003cffffffff99805daf\u003e] driver_probe_device+0x1f/0x90     [\u003cffffffff9980601e\u003e] __driver_attach+0xce/0x1c0     [\u003cffffffff99803170\u003e] bus_for_each_dev+0x70/0xc0     [\u003cffffffff99804822\u003e] bus_add_driver+0x112/0x210     [\u003cffffffff99807245\u003e] driver_register+0x55/0x100     [\u003cffffffff9aee4acb\u003e] acpi_processor_driver_init+0x3b/0xc0     [\u003cffffffff990012d1\u003e] do_one_initcall+0x41/0x300     [\u003cffffffff9ae7c4b0\u003e] kernel_init_freeable+0x320/0x470     [\u003cffffffff99b231f6\u003e] kernel_init+0x16/0x1b0     [\u003cffffffff99042e6d\u003e] ret_from_fork+0x2d/0x50  Fix this by freeing the CPU idle device after unregistering it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26894\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26894](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26894)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26894**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26894](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26894)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "6.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26898-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26898 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  aoe: fix the potential use-after-free problem in aoecmd_cfg_pkts  This patch is against CVE-2023-6270. The description of cve is:    A flaw was found in the ATA over Ethernet (AoE) driver in the Linux   kernel. The aoecmd_cfg_pkts() function improperly updates the refcnt on   `struct net_device`, and a use-after-free can be triggered by racing   between the free on the struct and the access through the `skbtxq`   global queue. This could lead to a denial of service condition or   potential code execution.  In aoecmd_cfg_pkts(), it always calls dev_put(ifp) when skb initial code is finished. But the net_device ifp will still be used in later tx()-\u003edev_queue_xmit() in kthread. Which means that the dev_put(ifp) should NOT be called in the success path of skb initial code in aoecmd_cfg_pkts(). Otherwise tx() may run into use-after-free because the net_device is freed.  This patch removed the dev_put(ifp) in the success path in aoecmd_cfg_pkts(), and added dev_put() after skb xmit in tx()."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26898\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26898](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26898)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26898**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26898](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26898)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-26901-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-26901 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  do_sys_name_to_handle(): use kzalloc() to fix kernel-infoleak  syzbot identified a kernel information leak vulnerability in do_sys_name_to_handle() and issued the following report [1].  [1] \"BUG: KMSAN: kernel-infoleak in instrument_copy_to_user include/linux/instrumented.h:114 [inline] BUG: KMSAN: kernel-infoleak in _copy_to_user+0xbc/0x100 lib/usercopy.c:40  instrument_copy_to_user include/linux/instrumented.h:114 [inline]  _copy_to_user+0xbc/0x100 lib/usercopy.c:40  copy_to_user include/linux/uaccess.h:191 [inline]  do_sys_name_to_handle fs/fhandle.c:73 [inline]  __do_sys_name_to_handle_at fs/fhandle.c:112 [inline]  __se_sys_name_to_handle_at+0x949/0xb10 fs/fhandle.c:94  __x64_sys_name_to_handle_at+0xe4/0x140 fs/fhandle.c:94  ...  Uninit was created at:  slab_post_alloc_hook+0x129/0xa70 mm/slab.h:768  slab_alloc_node mm/slub.c:3478 [inline]  __kmem_cache_alloc_node+0x5c9/0x970 mm/slub.c:3517  __do_kmalloc_node mm/slab_common.c:1006 [inline]  __kmalloc+0x121/0x3c0 mm/slab_common.c:1020  kmalloc include/linux/slab.h:604 [inline]  do_sys_name_to_handle fs/fhandle.c:39 [inline]  __do_sys_name_to_handle_at fs/fhandle.c:112 [inline]  __se_sys_name_to_handle_at+0x441/0xb10 fs/fhandle.c:94  __x64_sys_name_to_handle_at+0xe4/0x140 fs/fhandle.c:94  ...  Bytes 18-19 of 20 are uninitialized Memory access of size 20 starts at ffff888128a46380 Data copied to user address 0000000020000240\"  Per Chuck Lever's suggestion, use kzalloc() instead of kmalloc() to solve the problem."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-26901\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-26901](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26901)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-26901**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-26901](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-26901)  |\n"
              },
