              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27043-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27043 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  media: edia: dvbdev: fix a use-after-free  In dvb_register_device, *pdvbdev is set equal to dvbdev, which is freed in several error-handling paths. However, *pdvbdev is not set to NULL after dvbdev's deallocation, causing use-after-frees in many places, for example, in the following call chain:  budget_register   |-\u003e dvb_dmxdev_init         |-\u003e dvb_register_device   |-\u003e dvb_dmxdev_release         |-\u003e dvb_unregister_device               |-\u003e dvb_remove_device                     |-\u003e dvb_device_put                           |-\u003e kref_put  When calling dvb_unregister_device, dmxdev-\u003edvbdev (i.e. *pdvbdev in dvb_register_device) could point to memory that had been freed in dvb_register_device. Thereafter, this pointer is transferred to kref_put and triggering a use-after-free."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27043\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-27043](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27043)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-27043**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-27043](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27043)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27046-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27046 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  nfp: flower: handle acti_netdevs allocation failure  The kmalloc_array() in nfp_fl_lag_do_work() will return null, if the physical memory has run out. As a result, if we dereference the acti_netdevs, the null pointer dereference bugs will happen.  This patch adds a check to judge whether allocation failure occurs. If it happens, the delayed work will be rescheduled and try again."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27046\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-27046](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27046)",
