            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27074-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27074 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  media: go7007: fix a memleak in go7007_load_encoder  In go7007_load_encoder, bounce(i.e. go-\u003eboot_fw), is allocated without a deallocation thereafter. After the following call chain:  saa7134_go7007_init   |-\u003e go7007_boot_encoder         |-\u003e go7007_load_encoder   |-\u003e kfree(go)  go is freed and thus bounce is leaked."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27074\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-27074](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27074)",
