              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27437-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27437 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  vfio/pci: Disable auto-enable of exclusive INTx IRQ  Currently for devices requiring masking at the irqchip for INTx, ie. devices without DisINTx support, the IRQ is enabled in request_irq() and subsequently disabled as necessary to align with the masked status flag.  This presents a window where the interrupt could fire between these events, resulting in the IRQ incrementing the disable depth twice. This would be unrecoverable for a user since the masked flag prevents nested enables through vfio.  Instead, invert the logic using IRQF_NO_AUTOEN such that exclusive INTx is never auto-enabled, then unmask as required."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27437\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-27437](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27437)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-27437**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-27437](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-27437)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27982-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-27982 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The team has identified a critical vulnerability in the http server of the most recent version of Node, where malformed headers can lead to HTTP request smuggling. Specifically, if a space is placed before a content-length header, it is not interpreted correctly, enabling attackers to smuggle in a second request within the body of the first."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
