              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35811-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35811 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  wifi: brcmfmac: Fix use-after-free bug in brcmf_cfg80211_detach  This is the candidate patch of CVE-2023-47233 : https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-47233  In brcm80211 driver,it starts with the following invoking chain to start init a timeout worker:  -\u003ebrcmf_usb_probe   -\u003ebrcmf_usb_probe_cb     -\u003ebrcmf_attach       -\u003ebrcmf_bus_started         -\u003ebrcmf_cfg80211_attach           -\u003ewl_init_priv             -\u003ebrcmf_init_escan               -\u003eINIT_WORK(\u0026cfg-\u003eescan_timeout_work, \t\t  brcmf_cfg80211_escan_timeout_worker);  If we disconnect the USB by hotplug, it will call brcmf_usb_disconnect to make cleanup. The invoking chain is :  brcmf_usb_disconnect   -\u003ebrcmf_usb_disconnect_cb     -\u003ebrcmf_detach       -\u003ebrcmf_cfg80211_detach         -\u003ekfree(cfg);  While the timeout woker may still be running. This will cause a use-after-free bug on cfg in brcmf_cfg80211_escan_timeout_worker.  Fix it by deleting the timer and canceling the worker in brcmf_cfg80211_detach.  [arend.vanspriel@broadcom.com: keep timer delete as is and cancel work just before free]"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35811\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-35811](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35811)",
