            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35823-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35823 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  vt: fix unicode buffer corruption when deleting characters  This is the same issue that was fixed for the VGA text buffer in commit 39cdb68c64d8 (\"vt: fix memory overlapping when deleting chars in the buffer\"). The cure is also the same i.e. replace memcpy() with memmove() due to the overlaping buffers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35823\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-35823](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35823)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-35823**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-35823](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35823)  |\n"
