            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35887-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35887 high vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  ax25: fix use-after-free bugs caused by ax25_ds_del_timer  When the ax25 device is detaching, the ax25_dev_device_down() calls ax25_ds_del_timer() to cleanup the slave_timer. When the timer handler is running, the ax25_ds_del_timer() that calls del_timer() in it will return directly. As a result, the use-after-free bugs could happen, one of the scenarios is shown below:        (Thread 1)          |      (Thread 2)                           | ax25_ds_timeout() ax25_dev_device_down()    |   ax25_ds_del_timer()     |     del_timer()           |   ax25_dev_put() //FREE   |                           |  ax25_dev-\u003e //USE  In order to mitigate bugs, when the device is detaching, use timer_shutdown_sync() to stop the timer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35887\nSeverity: high\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-35887](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35887)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-35887**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-35887](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35887)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
