            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35928-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35928 low vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  drm/amd/amdgpu: Fix potential ioremap() memory leaks in amdgpu_device_init()  This ensures that the memory mapped by ioremap for adev-\u003ermmio, is properly handled in amdgpu_device_init(). If the function exits early due to an error, the memory is unmapped. If the function completes successfully, the memory remains mapped.  Reported by smatch: drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c:4337 amdgpu_device_init() warn: 'adev-\u003ermmio' from ioremap() not released on lines: 4035,4045,4051,4058,4068,4337"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35928\nSeverity: low\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-35928](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35928)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-35928**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  |   | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-35928](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35928)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "0.0"
