            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-35935-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-35935 low vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  btrfs: send: handle path ref underflow in header iterate_inode_ref()  Change BUG_ON to proper error handling if building the path buffer fails. The pointers are not printed so we don't accidentally leak kernel addresses."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-35935\nSeverity: low\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-35935](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35935)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-35935**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-35935](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-35935)  |\n"
