              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  drm/amd/display: Skip on writeback when it's not applicable  [WHY] dynamic memory safety error detector (KASAN) catches and generates error messages \"BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds\" as writeback connector does not support certain features which are not initialized.  [HOW] Skip them when connector type is DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_WRITEBACK."
