            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-38634-linux-libc-dev",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-38634 medium vulnerability for linux-libc-dev package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  serial: max3100: Lock port-\u003elock when calling uart_handle_cts_change()  uart_handle_cts_change() has to be called with port lock taken, Since we run it in a separate work, the lock may not be taken at the time of running. Make sure that it's taken by explicitly doing that. Without it we got a splat:    WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 10 at drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c:3491 uart_handle_cts_change+0xa6/0xb0   ...   Workqueue: max3100-0 max3100_work [max3100]   RIP: 0010:uart_handle_cts_change+0xa6/0xb0   ...    max3100_handlerx+0xc5/0x110 [max3100]    max3100_work+0x12a/0x340 [max3100]"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-38634\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nVersion: 4.19.289-2\nFix Version: 4.19.316-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:10\nLink: [CVE-2024-38634](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-38634)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-38634**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | linux-libc-dev  | 4.19.289-2  | 4.19.316-1  | deb  | /usr/share/doc/linux-libc-dev/copyright  | debian:distro:debian:10  | [CVE-2024-38634](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-38634)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
