            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-23085-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-23085 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A memory leak could occur when a remote peer abruptly closes the socket without sending a GOAWAY notification. Additionally, if an invalid header was detected by nghttp2, causing the connection to be terminated by the peer, the same leak was triggered. This flaw could lead to increased memory consumption and potential denial of service under certain conditions.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability affects HTTP/2 Server users on Node.js v18.x, v20.x, v22.x and v23.x."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-23085\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 18.20.6,20.18.2,22.13.1,23.6.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-23085](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23085)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-23085**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | node  | 16.20.2  | 18.20.6,20.18.2,22.13.1,23.6.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-23085](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23085)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-23165-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-23165 low vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In Node.js, the `ReadFileUtf8` internal binding leaks memory due to a corrupted pointer in `uv_fs_s.file`: a UTF-16 path buffer is allocated but subsequently overwritten when the file descriptor is set. This results in an unrecoverable memory leak on every call. Repeated use can cause unbounded memory growth, leading to a denial of service.\r\n\r\nImpact:\r\n* This vulnerability affects APIs relying on `ReadFileUtf8` on Node.js release lines: v20 and v22."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-23165\nSeverity: low\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.19.2,22.15.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-23165](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23165)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-23165**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | node  | 16.20.2  | 20.19.2,22.15.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-23165](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23165)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "3.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-23166-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-23166 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The C++ method SignTraits::DeriveBits() may incorrectly call ThrowException() based on user-supplied inputs when executing in a background thread, crashing the Node.js process. Such cryptographic operations are commonly applied to untrusted inputs. Thus, this mechanism potentially allows an adversary to remotely crash a Node.js runtime."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-23166\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.19.2,22.15.1,23.11.1,24.0.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-23166](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23166)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-23166**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 16.20.2  | 20.19.2,22.15.1,23.11.1,24.0.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-23166](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23166)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-23167-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-23167 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in Node.js 20's HTTP parser allows improper termination of HTTP/1 headers using `\\r\\n\\rX` instead of the required `\\r\\n\\r\\n`.\nThis inconsistency enables request smuggling, allowing attackers to bypass proxy-based access controls and submit unauthorized requests.\n\nThe issue was resolved by upgrading `llhttp` to version 9, which enforces correct header termination.\n\nImpact:\n* This vulnerability affects only Node.js 20.x users prior to the `llhttp` v9 upgrade."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-23167\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.19.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-23167](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23167)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-23167**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | node  | 16.20.2  | 20.19.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-23167](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-23167)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-55131-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-55131 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in Node.js's buffer allocation logic can expose uninitialized memory when allocations are interrupted, when using the `vm` module with the timeout option. Under specific timing conditions, buffers allocated with `Buffer.alloc` and other `TypedArray` instances like `Uint8Array` may contain leftover data from previous operations, allowing in-process secrets like tokens or passwords to leak or causing data corruption. While exploitation typically requires precise timing or in-process code execution, it can become remotely exploitable when untrusted input influences workload and timeouts, leading to potential confidentiality and integrity impact."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-55131\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-55131](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-55131)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-55131**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 16.20.2  | 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-55131](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-55131)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59465-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59465 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malformed `HTTP/2 HEADERS` frame with oversized, invalid `HPACK` data can cause Node.js to crash by triggering an unhandled `TLSSocket` error `ECONNRESET`. Instead of safely closing the connection, the process crashes, enabling a remote denial of service. This primarily affects applications that do not attach explicit error handlers to secure sockets, for example:\n```\nserver.on('secureConnection', socket =\u003e {\n  socket.on('error', err =\u003e {\n    console.log(err)\n  })\n})\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59465\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-59465](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59465)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59465**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 16.20.2  | 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-59465](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59465)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59466-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59466 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "We have identified a bug in Node.js error handling where \"Maximum call stack size exceeded\" errors become uncatchable when `async_hooks.createHook()` is enabled. Instead of reaching `process.on('uncaughtException')`, the process terminates, making the crash unrecoverable. Applications that rely on `AsyncLocalStorage` (v22, v20) or `async_hooks.createHook()` (v24, v22, v20) become vulnerable to denial-of-service crashes triggered by deep recursion under specific conditions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59466\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 16.20.2\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-59466](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59466)",
